<title>SINGAPORE: Acma 1996 net profit falls 23 pct.</title>
<headline>Acma 1996 net profit falls 23 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			     40.59 vs   52.78</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)			5.55 vs    5.55</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		    24.50 vs   31.90</p>
<p>    Group shr fully diluted (cents)  22.80 vs   31.90</p>
<p>    Turnover				559.20 vs  518.14</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest	 2.19 vs    2.35</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		    6.50 vs    2.15</p>
<p>    Depreciation/amortisation	  10.29 vs    8.54</p>
<p>    Profits from associates	     1.65 vs    5.36</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			 63.61 vs   78.66</p>
<p>    Tax					15.91 vs   22.73</p>
<p>    Minorities (losses)		   8.76 vs    8.51</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries			10.64 vs    4.62</p>
<p>    Dividend pay date:		    July 22, 1997</p>
<p>    Last day books open:		  June 8, 1997</p>
<p>Note - Acma Ltd manufactures electronics and computer parts. -- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
